                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3901e57b-0add-3df4-a7a8-09c23fbc42f6",
                        "entry_id": "d03bcafc-814e-30dd-a6a0-6c60f916858b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Balaeniceps rex, duży afrykański ptak o krótkim, silnym i masywnym dziobie, żywiący się wyłącznie rybami dwudysznymi"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "46ece6cc-b63b-44eb-b340-ffe84a7d006e",
                        "source_entry_id": "d03bcafc-814e-30dd-a6a0-6c60f916858b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3901e57b-0add-3df4-a7a8-09c23fbc42f6",
                        "target_lang_word": "shoebill",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shoebill",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                        "entry_id": "f8c46393-50b9-37a4-b7b4-08ac6e7d79ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Balaeniceps rex, a tall wading bird related to the stork, native to tropical African swamps; the sole species of the family Balaenicipitidae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "791e51b3-7b02-40c1-9b7d-f63130774fec",
                                                "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                                "text": "The Shoebill is distinctive in many aspects of its biology, and is thus, we feel, most appropriately placed in its own family, the Balaenicipitidae (L. Buxton et al. 1978, Kahl 1979a). The fact that we have included it in this book, while excluding the Hamerkop, indicates that we believe the Shoebill to be closer to the storks (Kahl 1967b, 1979c); however the jury remains out as to how close."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a48c2550-9e23-49d7-ab3c-f65608ff08bb",
                                                "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, Birdlife International recently classified it as near-globally threatened, and it is classed as CITES Appendix 2, which means that trade in shoebills, or their capture for any harmful activity, is forbidden by international law."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fabf0ed4-f72a-4cd9-8c0f-e9bfca41ec57",
                                                "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                                "text": "The monstrous and awesome shoebill is possibly the most bizarre bird on the African continent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9898d30f-fc24-468f-852a-7339dfb93e0c",
                        "source_entry_id": "d03bcafc-814e-30dd-a6a0-6c60f916858b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3901e57b-0add-3df4-a7a8-09c23fbc42f6",
                        "target_lang_word": "bec-en-sabot",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bec-en-sabot",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fc42979-bdc4-36d7-b610-2afcacf17c59",
                                        "entry_id": "20965462-51d7-39f7-84b9-6a704cd6f4cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Genre monotypique de grand oiseau échassier (Balaeniceps) de l'ordre des pélécaniformes et de la famille des balaénicipitidés, dont la seule espèce vivante est le bec-en-sabot du Nil ou abu-markub (Balaeniceps rex)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60119666-cf6e-418c-8379-26dbdcc622c0",
                        "source_entry_id": "d03bcafc-814e-30dd-a6a0-6c60f916858b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3901e57b-0add-3df4-a7a8-09c23fbc42f6",
                        "target_lang_word": "Schuhschnabel",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Schuhschnabel",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f980ef83-f173-39a8-9117-a4439edcb868",
                                        "entry_id": "000d8a15-157c-39f9-959e-0fc5f40dc48f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in mit Papyrus und Schilf durchwachsenen Sümpfe, Fluss- und Seeufer Südsudans, Ugandas, Tansanias, Sambias und vereinzelt angrenzender Länder lebender graublau gefiederter, großköpfiger Vogel mit einem auffällig großen und breiten, gelbbraunen Schnabel, dessen Form an die eines Holzschuhs erinnert (Balaeniceps rex)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4823ca57-427b-48d1-b2d6-255307d5579d",
                                                "sense_id": "f980ef83-f173-39a8-9117-a4439edcb868",
                                                "text": "Der Schuhschnabel lebt versteckt im Röhricht."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27917c38-6e99-49e3-98a1-2e0afa849164",
                                                "sense_id": "f980ef83-f173-39a8-9117-a4439edcb868",
                                                "text": "„Er hat zum ersten Male Schuhschnäbel gefilmt, aber Nester mit Jungen hat auch er nicht gefunden. Noch kein Europäer hat einen brütenden Schuhschnabel erblickt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb9f94eb-8401-4f58-b68d-267d74f21417",
                                                "sense_id": "f980ef83-f173-39a8-9117-a4439edcb868",
                                                "text": "«Die Heimat des Schuhschnabels sind die Papyrussümpfe des oberen Weissen Nils und anderer Flüsse in Ostafrika.»"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9d7039e-215b-4465-8bde-94d1cd8a8bb2",
                                                "sense_id": "f980ef83-f173-39a8-9117-a4439edcb868",
                                                "text": "„Das Verhalten ist grausam, aber unter großen Vögeln weitverbreitet: Die ältesten Küken des Schuhschnabels etwa quälen ihre jüngeren Geschwister mit Schnabelhieben und Federnrupfen bis zum Tode.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ee48692c-c7fa-4d6f-9b6d-481ed45740b7",
                        "source_entry_id": "d03bcafc-814e-30dd-a6a0-6c60f916858b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3901e57b-0add-3df4-a7a8-09c23fbc42f6",
